        "testata": "France 24",
        "lingua_originale": "en",
        "titolo_orig": "Trump calls off latest threats to strike Iran, citing progress in negotiations",
        "testo_it": "Il presidente USA Trump revoca le minacce di attacco all'Iran, segnalando progressi nei negoziati bilaterali.",
        "priorita": "Altissima",
        "id_gruppo": 4,
        "link": "https://www.france24.com/en/trump-calls-off-latest-threats-to-strike-iran-citing-progress-in-negotiations",
        "orario": "21:22",
        "timestamp": 1781205764,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Trump calls off latest threats to strike Iran, citing progress in negotiations Middle East Issued on: 11/06/2026 - 21:22 President Donald Trump called off new U.S. military strikes on Iran on Thursday, saying \"final points\" of an initial peace deal had been approved and details of a signing ​ceremony would ‌be announced shortly. Iran's semi-official Fars news agency reported that Tehran had not approved ⁠the text of any agreement. Since mid-March, Trump has repeatedly claimed that a deal with Iran to ‌end the war is close. FRANCE 24's Carys Garland and Monte Francis report. 'Our worries are increasing day by day': A Lebanese family lives through wartime 11/06/2026 On the ground Middle East Three Indian crew missing as US says fired on tanker off Oman 10/06/2026 Middle East Israeli airstrikes kill 13 in south Lebanon, Lebanese sources say 10/06/2026 Middle East US-Iran deal 'wouldn't resolve anything': Trump trapped between 'unwinnable war, unpresentable deal' 10/06/2026 Middle East Trump vows response after Iran shoots down US helicopter 09/06/2026 Middle East Lebanon says 8 dead in strike on Tyre as Israel keeps up attacks on south 09/06/2026 Middle East France bans Israeli minister Smotrich in coordinated sanctions push 09/06/2026 Middle East Israel continues strikes on Beirut suburb 09/06/2026 Middle East Trump remains optimistic peace deal can be reached despite Middle East flare-up 09/06/2026 Middle East"
